{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788132822,"nonce":"EDvMePask59j91WKdu6n4avK84U=","message":"AMENDMENT from the action-surface + curriculum audits — orchestrator, session 4.\nScope additions, all verified at file:line in the decompiled 1.6 tree. Nothing\nhere is a rewrite; the spec's existing scope stands.\n\n**1. STOP DEFERRING prisoner/guest/slave state.** The body says \"wardens\ninteract … minimal prisoner ops *if cheap*; else defer to a later wave\". It is\ncheap — every one is a field write or a two-line method — and **M3 rides on it**,\nbecause M3 is Factions/**Guests** with the Hospitality cluster, and guest status\nplus prisoner interaction mode are precisely the state that suite overloads.\nDeferring this defers M3.\n- `Pawn_GuestTracker.SetExclusiveInteraction` (`RimWorld/Pawn_GuestTracker.cs:304`),\n  `ToggleNonExclusiveInteraction` (`:316`), `SetNoInteraction` (`:362`)\n- `SetGuestStatus(faction, GuestStatus)` (`:443`) — the guest⇄prisoner⇄slave transition\n- `slaveInteractionMode` (`:17`), `Recruitable` (`:214`), conversion ideo (`:51`)\n- 12 modes at `RimWorld/PrisonerInteractionModeDefOf.cs:6-35`\n- The tab is `ITab_Pawn_Visitor`; `ITab_Pawn_Prisoner`/`ITab_Pawn_Guest` are\n  12- and 22-line subclasses of it.\n\n**2. Emergency orders — DESIGN §Observation layer 4 says the agent \"intervenes\nby exception\", and there is currently no exception verb.** All absent, all M1:\n- extinguish fires near a cell — `FloatMenuOptionProvider_ExtinguishFires.cs:16`\n- beat out fire on a burning pawn — `FloatMenuOptionProvider_PutOutFireOnPawn.cs:14`\n- drafted tend, with/without medicine, incl. self — `FloatMenuOptionProvider_DraftedTend.cs:30`\n- man a turret — `CompMannable.cs:55`\n- use medical bed / rest until healed — `Building_Bed.cs:594`, job at `:620`\n- fire-at-will toggle — `Pawn_DraftController.cs:199`\n- drafted repair — `FloatMenuOptionProvider_DraftedRepair.cs:27`\n`Alert_FireInHomeArea` is standing vanilla, and firefighting via work priorities\ndoes not cover a fire that starts at 3am in the power room.\n\n**3. `prioritize {job} on {thing}` understates the surface three ways.**\n(a) `WorkGiverDef.directOrderable` defaults **true** (`RimWorld/WorkGiverDef.cs:32`),\nso essentially every `WorkGiver_Scanner` is a right-click order.\n(b) There is a **cell**-target form as well as a thing form\n(`FloatMenuOptionProvider_WorkGivers.cs:29` vs `:43`) — \"sow this area\", \"mine this area\".\n(c) It routes through `TryTakeOrderedJobPrioritizedWork`\n(`Verse.AI/Pawn_JobTracker.cs:877`), which writes `pawn.mindState.priorityWork`\n(`:883`) when `prioritizeSustains` — a **durable state mutation**, not a one-shot\njob. The flat phrasing hides all three.\n\n**4. Order availability is gated on selection state and the parity list omits\nit.** `FloatMenuOptionProvider.Drafted/Undrafted/Multiselect/RequiresManipulation/\nMechanoidCanDo` (`RimWorld/FloatMenuOptionProvider.cs:8-16`). Clean-room and\nromance are undrafted-only; tend, repair, carry-pawn and corpse-handling are\ndrafted-only. A verb that ignores the gate silently no-ops.\n\n**5. Research project selection belongs here** (one call, no window):\n`ResearchManager.SetCurrentProject` (`RimWorld/ResearchManager.cs:110`),\n`StopProject` (`:132`). Only `dev:finish-research` exists today and 4.3 bans dev\nverbs after staging. **It does NOT check `CanStartNow`** (`Verse/ResearchProjectDef.cs:164`)\n— reproduce that per DESIGN's widget-gate invariant. Both audits flagged this\nindependently; `Alert_NeedResearchProject` has already fired on our fixtures.\n\n**6. A `flick` verb.** `CompFlickable` only sets `wantSwitchOn` and adds a Flick\ndesignation (`RimWorld/CompFlickable.cs:113-124`); a pawn must walk over and do\nit. **So power on/off is ASYNCHRONOUS** — `SwitchIsOn` (`:38`) does not move\nuntil the job runs. A verb that returns \"power off\" immediately is lying; echo\nthe designation, not the state. The game has a whole concept for this\n(`SwitchFlickingDesignation`) precisely because players get it wrong.\n\n**7. Cheaper than the spec assumes:** copy/paste a whole work-priority row or\ntimetable row between pawns is ONE call\n(`RimWorld/PawnColumnWorker_CopyPasteWorkPriorities.cs:43`). The \"matrix or\nper-pawn\" open question should include \"or copied from another pawn\".\n\n**8. Reading policies** are a fifth policy database with the same shape as the\nfour named (`Dialog_ManageReadingPolicies`, `PawnColumnWorker_Reading`). Minor.\n\n**Undraft is its own step.** The scripted tutorial has a dedicated `UndraftAll`\ninstruction and the `Drafting` concept warns \"don't leave colonists Drafted\nforever - they'll starve and become unhappy\". 4.2's emergency posture never\ncloses that loop; raised there too.","files":null}]}